    exampleTitle: "Build a gimmick that blushes when your head is patted",
    exampleLead: `Put a Receiver above your head so your cheeks turn redder the closer a hand or finger gets. Set the Receiver Type to Proximity, and use Motion Time to turn the closeness into the strength of the blush. How to build the Animator is explained in ${tipLink("toggle")}, and Motion Time in ${tipLink("radial", "float")}.`,
    receiverLabel: "1. Place the Receiver",
    receiver: [
      "In the Hierarchy, expand your avatar and find the head bone (Head) inside the Armature. The names and order differ by avatar (e.g. <code>Armature → Hips → Spine → Chest → Neck → Head</code>).",
      "Right-click Head and choose <code>Create Empty</code>. Name the new GameObject <code>HeadPat</code>. You make it a child of the head bone so the Receiver follows your head when it moves.",
      "With <code>HeadPat</code> selected, press <code>Add Component</code> at the bottom of the Inspector, type <code>VRC Contact Receiver</code> and add it.",
      "Set <code>Shape Type</code> to <code>Sphere</code> and <code>Radius</code> to about 0.1 to 0.15. A sphere outline appears in the Scene view. Raise the Y of <code>Position</code> a little so the sphere covers the top of your head. The values depend on your avatar's size, so decide while looking at the Scene view.",
      "Check <code>Allow Others</code>. If you also want it to react when you pat yourself, check <code>Allow Self</code> too. Leave <code>Local Only</code> unchecked (the reason is explained below in \"Does everyone see the same thing?\").",
      "Press <code>Add</code> under <code>Collision Tags</code> and choose <code>Hand</code> from the list. Press it again and add <code>Finger</code> too. If you type them in, match upper and lower case exactly.",
      "Set <code>Receiver Type</code> to <code>Proximity</code> and type <code>HeadPat</code> in <code>Parameter</code>.",
    ],
    receiverMock: {
      variant: "unity",
      caption: "Recreated view: Unity's Inspector (VRC Contact Receiver). Names are examples.",
      screens: [{
        bar: "Inspector › HeadPat (VRC Contact Receiver)",
        label: "Recreated view of VRC Contact Receiver. 1 Shape Type Sphere, Radius 0.12, 2 Allow Self off, Allow Others on, Local Only off, 3 Collision Tags are Hand and Finger, 4 Receiver Type Proximity, Parameter HeadPat",
        rows: [
          { type: "head", text: "Shape" },
          { mark: 1, label: "Shape Type", type: "select", text: "Sphere" },
          { label: "Radius", type: "value", text: "0.12" },
          { label: "Position", type: "value", text: "X 0 · Y 0.1 · Z 0" },
          { type: "head", text: "Filtering" },
          { mark: 2, type: "check", on: false, text: "Allow Self" },
