    sync2: [
      "Use Local Only for reactions you don't need to show others (like a sound only you hear). Don't use it for reactions you want to show, like a blush.",
      `If you also add a parameter with the same name to Expression Parameters and sync it, it becomes unclear on other people's screens whether the value sent to them or the value their own VRChat got from the Contact is used. Don't add it at first. If you really want everyone to see exactly the same value, there's a way to copy a Local Only Receiver's value into a synced parameter with VRC Avatar Parameter Driver, but that's for advanced users. See also ${tipLink("radial", "sync")} for how syncing works.`,
